  "notes": [
    "stopIds (array, both directional platform ids) populated 5 Sep 2026 via scripts/enrich-wm-metro-stop-ids.mjs, TfWM-code-verified against both the GTFS static feed and a live trip_updates pull. Legacy singular stopId is deliberately left null — TfWM's feed keys stop_time_update.stop_id by platform, not by station, so a single scalar can't represent both directions without silently dropping one; see docs/uk-west-midlands-d1/oracle-clash-report.md's 5 Sep addendum and the script's header comment for the adapter follow-up this unblocks (accept stopIds[], merge trips).",
    "stationId (reference only, GTFS parent/location_type=1 id) never appears in the live trip_updates feed — do not filter on it.",
    "Do not use CRS for Metro stops. catalogId disambiguates NR interchanges (Grand Central vs BHM, Wolverhampton Station vs WVH).",
    "Wednesbury–Brierley Hill / Dudley extension stops are out until operator lists under Current Service.",
    "This file records TfWM's own published stop names verbatim and is deliberately NOT renamed. Three of these names (Five Ways, Jewellery Quarter, The Hawthorns) collide with a National Rail station of the same printed name already in this region's catalog; lib/cities/uk-west-midlands/stations.json's catalog entries for those three are suffixed \"(Metro)\" to disambiguate (6 Sep 2026, see docs/uk-west-midlands-d1/oracle-clash-report.md's 6 Sep addendum). The adapter (lib/providers/uk-metro-wm.js) resolves stops via the stations.json catalog entry's catalogId/stopIds, never by matching this file's `name` field directly, so no mapping field is needed here."
  ],
